@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+/* Copyright 2026 The Sunshine OS contributors
+ * Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
+ * found in the LICENSE file.
+ *
+ * This stylesheet declares no colour, for the two reasons
+ * chrome/browser/resources/sunshine/document_content/app.css gives at length
+ * and which apply here without change.
+ *
+ * It cannot: chrome://theme is not reachable from a chrome-untrusted://
+ * origin, so a colour here would be either a new theme source on an untrusted
+ * origin or a literal, and docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM_CONTRACT.md section 2.3 requires
+ * a colour that escapes the theme to fail visibly rather than be papered over.
+ *
+ * It should not: a module app is content, not chrome. Lending it the browser's
+ * own palette would let a mounted module imitate the shell that embeds it,
+ * which is the confusion the shell/frame split exists to prevent. That matters
+ * more for a module than for a document, because a module is authored
+ * elsewhere and may be authored by anyone.
+ *
+ * What is left is layout, in rem, on the section 6.2 scale. */
+
+body {
+  margin: 0;
+}
+
+#body {
+  display: block;
+  padding: 1rem;
+}
+
+h1 {
+  font-size: 1rem;
+  line-height: 1.5;
+  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
+}
+
+p {
+  font-size: 0.875rem;
+  line-height: 1.43;
+  margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
+}
+
+ul {
+  font-size: 0.875rem;
+  line-height: 1.43;
+  margin: 0;
+  padding-inline-start: 1.5rem;
+}
